        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: मध्याह्नः",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मध्याह्नः (madhyāhnaḥ) — \"noon\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मध्याह्नः (madhyāhnaḥ) is midday, the sun at the top of its climb."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is two pieces joined: madhya, \"middle\", and ahan, a day. Sanskrit keeps more than one word for a day, and this is the other one — दिनम् is the day you count, ahan the day you are standing in. English mid is madhya's own worn-down cousin."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "So noon is the middle of the day said in one breath, which is what noon is in most languages once you take the word apart."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The top of the day, between its two ends."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
