        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: मासः",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मासः (māsaḥ) — \"a month\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मासः (māsaḥ) is a month, and it is the moon's own word."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You have चन्द्रः for the moon overhead. मासः (māsaḥ) is that same moon counted: the stretch from one to the next."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Latin mēnsis, Greek mēn, English month and moon are all one word travelled west, and this is among the securest cousins in the whole family. Ends in -अः."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A stretch of time measured by the moon you already know."
            }
          ]
        },
